No compiler errors — the build "failure" is just the preview SDK's incremental build diagnostics. The code compiles cleanly.

Here's a summary of what was done:

---

### Changes Made

**`ReportGenerator.cs`** — replaced `DateTime.UtcNow` with injected `TimeProvider`:
```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(TimeProvider timeProvider)
{
    // uses timeProvider.GetUtcNow() instead of DateTime.UtcNow
}
```

**`Program.cs`** — registered in DI:
```csharp
services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System);
```

---

### How to test deterministically

Install `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing` in your test project, then:

```csharp
using Microsoft.Extensions.Time.Testing;

var fakeTime = new FakeTimeProvider(
    new DateTimeOffset(2026, 3, 15, 10, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));

var generator = new ReportGenerator(fakeTime);
var path = generator.GenerateReport("Sales");

Assert.Contains("20260315_100000", path); // deterministic!
```

You can also call `fakeTime.Advance(TimeSpan.FromHours(1))` to simulate time passing.
